From 61c923da684b15866bbbfe5c71cf83bc56676591 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:53:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs(claims): say only what the goldens, the matrix test and
 the 2026-10-15 resume runs prove

The README support table gets a "Verified (2026-10-15)" column in place of
feature notes. Claude Code, Codex CLI, Pi and Copilot CLI keep a resume
check because an installed agent (claude 2.1.285, codex-cli 0.162.1, pi
0.84.3, copilot CLI 1.0.61) answered from the projected history; Gemini CLI
0.47.0 and opencode 1.18.18 only rendered the projection, and Cursor 3.24.12
only opens the workspace with the composer listed, so their cells say that.
Gemini's "reasoning tokens round-trip losslessly", Codex's "every file
change", Pi's "branching trees", Claude's "rotated files merged" are scoped
to the unit test or crate fixture that covers them; the opencode snapshot
diff claim is marked implemented and untested (no test calls diff_trees);
"copilot 1.0.67" becomes the version that resumed today, with the earlier
run noted as predating the fixes it needed (74f805f, 23f48da); "in CI" is
dropped because no workflow on main runs the tests.

The site front page stops saying "any agent", "everything the last one
knew", "the full session" and "resumes natively"; it lists the agents and
versions that resumed, rendered, or opened. crates.json roles for codex,
copilot, opencode, pi, gemini and cursor carry the same scoping, including
the gemini 0.47 .jsonl and Cursor 3.24 header-table gaps the reader has.
The copilot, cursor and gemini format notes get dated observations from
the resume matrices. Evidence: review/claims-audit.md in the scratchpad.
