From 5f82a352a868f7e680841dab7b2368c2c6a67787 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:54:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs(kinds): agent-coding-session v1.1.0 is the only version
 producers write; v1.0.0 is read-only legacy

The kinds index gains a Status column with one row per version: v1.1.0
"current, the only version producers write"; v1.0.0 "read-only legacy,
superseded 2026-06-17, not supported for writing, path p validate warns".
The kind landing page, the v1.0.0 page (a Status entry in its header), the
v1.1.0 page, the README's kind paragraph and the RFC's Document Kind
section say the same thing in their own words. The RFC previously named
v1.0.0 as the only defined kind, which has been false since 2026-06-17.
The legacy constant's doc comment in toolpath::v1 states the rule and
points at the test that enforces it.

"Not supported for writing" is a rule for producers, not a change to the
format: the URI stays immutable and documents carrying it stay valid, so
readers keep accepting them and validation warns instead of rejecting.
