From 4a3d18c73343e1d392c73b72fef3bb2411fcd625 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:02:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] path-cli: every producer writes kind v1.1.0 (test), and `p
 validate` warns on a v1.0.0 document
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two tests in cross_harness_matrix.rs: `every_producer_writes_the_current_kind`
derives each of the seven captured fixtures once through `derive_path` (the
one place the kind is stamped, which every provider crate's wrapper calls)
and asserts `meta.kind` is the current constant, which must end in v1.1.0;
`no_source_spells_the_superseded_kind_outside_the_legacy_constant` scans
every crate's `src/` for the v1.0.0 URI and allows it only in
toolpath/src/types.rs, where the legacy constant lives. The one other
spelling, a selector test in kinds.rs, now uses the constant.

`path p validate` prints `warning: path <id> has kind <v1.0.0 URI> …` on
stderr for each inline path carrying the legacy kind, naming the erratum and
the current URI, and still exits 0 with `Valid:`. It warns rather than
rejects because kind URIs are immutable and documents written against an
old one stay valid by the format's own rule; the bundled v1.0.0 schema still
validates them, and every document cached or uploaded before 2026-06-17
carries that kind. Unit tests cover one warning per legacy path, none for
the current kind or a kindless path, and that the legacy document still
validates.
---
 crates/path-cli/src/cmd_validate.rs           | 92 ++++++++++++++++++-
 crates/path-cli/src/kinds.rs                  |  4 +-
 crates/path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs | 89 +++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 182 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

